# Workflow

Purpose:
  The .sdd system's workflow layer. Contains the workflow engine
  (stages, transitions, gates, state machine) and workflow
  implementations (migration, feature-planning, agent-workflow, etc.).

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @stages.sdd (formal stage registry)
   3 @transitions.sdd (default and conditional transitions)
   4 @gates.sdd (gate criteria for each stage)
   5 @state.sdd (task state machine)
   6 @lifecycle.sdd (workflow lifecycle)
   7 @policies.sdd (workflow policies)
   8 @testing.sdd (test levels T0-T7, test pyramid)
   9 @dependencies.sdd (workflow dependencies)
   10 @engine-recovery.sdd (workflow engine recovery)
   11 @impl-migration.sdd (migration workflow)
   12 @impl-feature-planning.sdd (feature planning workflow)
   13 @impl-agent-workflow.sdd (agent workflow)
   14 @impl-agent-implementation.sdd (agent implementation workflow)
   15 @impl-chain-implementation.sdd (chain implementation workflow)
   16 @impl-task-execution.sdd (task execution workflow)
   17 @impl-recovery.sdd (task execution recovery)
   18 @impl-parallel-execution.sdd (parallel execution workflow)
   19 @impl-knowledge-sharing.sdd (knowledge sharing workflow)
   20 @impl-intelligent-runtime.sdd (intelligent runtime workflow)
   21 @impl-backup-integrity.sdd (backup integrity workflow)
   22 @impl-skill-auto-integration.sdd (skill auto-integration workflow)
   23 @impl-example-prompt-to-code.sdd (example prompt-to-code workflow)

Navigation:
  Engine:
    Stages: @stages.sdd
    Transitions: @transitions.sdd
    Gates: @gates.sdd
    State: @state.sdd
    Lifecycle: @lifecycle.sdd
    Policies: @policies.sdd
    Testing: @testing.sdd
    Dependencies: @dependencies.sdd
    Recovery: @engine-recovery.sdd
  Implementations:
    Migration: @impl-migration.sdd
    FeaturePlanning: @impl-feature-planning.sdd
    AgentWorkflow: @impl-agent-workflow.sdd
    AgentImplementation: @impl-agent-implementation.sdd
    ChainImplementation: @impl-chain-implementation.sdd
    TaskExecution: @impl-task-execution.sdd
    Recovery: @impl-recovery.sdd
    ParallelExecution: @impl-parallel-execution.sdd
    KnowledgeSharing: @impl-knowledge-sharing.sdd
    IntelligentRuntime: @impl-intelligent-runtime.sdd
    BackupIntegrity: @impl-backup-integrity.sdd
    SkillAutoIntegration: @impl-skill-auto-integration.sdd
    ExamplePromptToCode: @impl-example-prompt-to-code.sdd
   External:
     Chains: @../chains/
     Tasks: @../tasks/
     Skills: @../skills/
     State: @../state/state.sdd
     Runtime: @../runtime/INDEX.sdd
     Flows: @flows/INDEX.sdd
     FlowFeature: @flows/feature.sdd

Rules:
  [W1]  AI MUST load workflow/INDEX.sdd before reading any workflow
        component — never read workflow files blindly.

  [W2]  A stage MUST be declared in stages.sdd before it can appear in
        any chain or transition.

  [W3]  A transition MUST reference valid source and target stages.

  [W4]  A gate MUST declare pass/fail criteria before the stage can
        advance.

  [W5]  State (workflow/state.sdd) and Stage (stages.sdd) are distinct
        concepts — a task at stage BE may be in state BLOCKED.

  [W6]  A task MUST NOT advance past a gate without passing it.

  [W7]  Test levels (T0-T7) are independent of stages — a stage MAY
        activate multiple test levels.

  [W8]  The task queue engine (NextAction) operates on task state, not
        stage — next valid transition determines next action.

  [W9]  Runtime events (events.sdd) MUST be appended, never modified —
        history is append-only.

  [W10] A workflow change (new stage, new transition, new gate) requires
        human approval if it affects an existing project's chains.
  [W11] Flow is fixed: BE->BE_TS->CR->FE->FE_TS->CR->MD->MD_TS->CR->BRU/CRU->MANUAL.
  [W12] BE_TS, FE_TS, MD_TS are test suite gates — they run only changed files.
  [W13] Full regression suites are NOT run on unchanged code — token economy rule.
  [W14] CR = Code Review — mandatory after each implementation stage and test suite.
  [W15] BRU = Business Requirement Unit — human-gated business validation.
  [W16] CRU = Code Requirement Unit — automated code quality and compliance check.
  [W17] MANUAL gate requires user login with full permissions from environment.
  [W18] /sdd next advances the decision chain to the next step automatically.
  [W19] Docker is the single execution environment — no host-level tool execution.
  [W20] Resource limits are enforced per Docker container: cpu, memory, pids, network.
  [W21] Docker MUST use local bind mounts — named volumes are forbidden.

State: +